                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "baf69566-2b6b-3506-830a-33a2c55dec38",
                        "entry_id": "82da3eab-1976-3796-a757-6d4834528693",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A proposition laid out previously; a proposition from which another proposition is inferred."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d23befca-34f4-42ff-83e5-760ffb1c6397",
                                "sense_id": "baf69566-2b6b-3506-830a-33a2c55dec38",
                                "text": "The subject of the prejacent and its exclusive must be one and the same (I grant that), but the subject of the prejacent ‘every man is a man’ is just ‘man’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8b0bc783-9f53-4b52-a406-4fcb67e796b2",
                                "sense_id": "baf69566-2b6b-3506-830a-33a2c55dec38",
                                "text": "I have suggested elsewhere (Horn 1992: 182-83) that this case requires an invocation of the notion of explicature or pragmatic enrichment […] so that the prejacent, while not constituting part of the linguistic meaning contributed by only, enters into the determination of what is said and hence into the enriched propositional content."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
